# The KL corpus is tokenized byte-for-byte, so its bytes must survive a round trip through git
# unchanged on every platform. With the repo's `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows these .txt files
# would otherwise be checked out with CRLF line endings, every "\n" would tokenize differently, and
# the committed tokens.json would no longer match a regeneration. `-text` disables all end-of-line
# conversion for this directory: what was committed is what is checked out.
#
# tokens.json is JSON and is pinned for the same reason (its sha256_of_token_ids_json values are
# compared against the sidecars both producers write).
* -text
